{"id": "EUVD-2026-101739", "enisaUuid": "81ea541e-0433-3961-a1b7-fffbfc8f3a69", "description": "GitPython before 3.2.0 contains a regular expression denial of service vulnerability in the _re_actor_epoch pattern used by parse_actor_and_date on author, committer, and tagger lines. Attackers can serve repositories with commit or tag objects containing long space-filled lines lacking a valid epoch or timezone, causing quadratic backtracking and CPU exhaustion.", "datePublished": "2026-10-14T22:52:38", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-20T02:25:27", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:N/VI:N/VA:H/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/gitpython-developers/GitPython/security/advisories/GHSA-m64x-33q8-m5h7", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/gitpython-before-3.2.0-redos-via-re-actor-epoch-in-parse-actor-and-date"], "aliases": ["GHSA-f52j-wg44-2h83", "CVE-2026-110856"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.28, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "9e30cf23-d0e1-3a63-8012-5303273bfa72", "product": {"name": "GitPython", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}, "product_version": "0 <3.2.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "50a23f89-2b31-3eb8-9edc-1d76f045b375", "vendor": {"name": "gitpython-developers"}}], "isExploited": false}